> What do these messages mean ?

These are just information from the driver, neither error not
warning.

> Oct 15 09:26:22 legolas kernel: ALSA sound/pci/hda/hda_intel.c:1185: =

> azx_pcm_prepare: bufsize=3D0x10000, fragsize=3D0x1000, format=3D0x11

The driver uses the buffer size 0x10000, fragment size 0x1000, and
chose format 0x11.

> Oct 15 09:26:22 legolas kernel: ALSA sound/pci/hda/hda_codec.c:623: =

> hda_codec_setup_stream: NID=3D0x13, stream=3D0x5, channel=3D0, format=3D0=
x11

The driver sets up the widget NID 0x13 for stream 0x5, channel 0 and
format 0x11.


